  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64370,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diffuse laminar endocervical hyperplasia is typically an incidental finding. An exophytic clinically visible lesion has been described {19820374}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64371,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 297,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a well-demarcated diffuse proliferation of typically round to oval but often irregular, angulated, or star-shaped endocervical glands. A dense acute and chronic inflammatory infiltrate with associated periglandular oedema may occur.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
